        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-23T16:31:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like we\u0027ve run into issues before where interrupts are enabled across the sysjump boundary: b/397656402\n\nI think using this on cortex-m is a safer change.\n```\n#define interrupt_disable_all() \\\n    irq_lock();\n    __disable_irq();\n```",
      "parentUuid": "f01a5f96_93aed71d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 28,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 28,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "b700ddcc4c0a012ee66521a9084c949acf47c6f0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "49c43c7a_7edc5a35",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 28,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-23T20:29:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "irq_lock() + __disable_irq() still leaves some cases uncovered. It results in `PRIMASK \u003d\u003d 1 \u0026\u0026 BASEPRI !\u003d 1`, which blocks priority interrupts from waking from WFI. This is problematic for hibernate (fixed in crrev/c/8623513). Also a problem for Zephyr -\u003e Legacy EC sysjumps because legacy EC does not clear BASEPRI (fixed by crrev/c/8645850 and crrev/c/8645849).\n\n`interrupt_disable_all()` is causing confusion. This CL replaces it with `irq_lock()` in most cases, except where special handling of interrupts is necessary (WFI and jumping to legacy EC).",
      "parentUuid": "4d02322a_af53454c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 28,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 28,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "b700ddcc4c0a012ee66521a9084c949acf47c6f0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
